course: dictionary
lesson: 943
title: Blocky: shapes, pictures and games
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Blocky describes something made of block shapes, with square edges and corners. It can also mean chunky and not smooth or detailed. Think of a tower of building bricks, or a picture made of big squares.
explain: «The kids laughed at the blocky graphics» in the story. The graphics are the pictures on a game screen, so the word tells you they looked chunky and square, not smooth. That is why the children laughed at them.
explain: Look at the words around a new word for clues. Words like building blocks or big squares tell you blocky means made of square shapes. Then try your meaning in the sentence: «the kids laughed at the chunky, square graphics» still makes sense, so you are on the right track.
fact: Blocky means made of block shapes, with square edges and corners.
fact: Blocky can also mean looking chunky and not smooth or detailed.
fact: Blocky is an adjective, so it describes a noun, such as a blocky model or a blocky picture.
fact: The comparing forms are blockier and blockiest.
fact: Pictures made of big squares, called pixels, can look blocky on a screen.
exercise: «The kids laughed at the blocky graphics.» What does blocky mean here? | *Chunky and square, not smooth | Wet and grey | Very quiet | Shiny and smooth
exercise: A model made of building bricks with square corners is best described as what? | Silent | *Blocky | Tiny and fragile | Smooth and round
exercise: «The model was built from blocky bricks, and it stood on the table.» Find and copy one word that describes the bricks. | *blocky | stood | table | model
test: Which is the best meaning of blocky? | Sung softly | Very bright and shiny | *Made of block shapes with square edges | Round and smooth
test: Which word compares the most blocky thing in a group of three? | *Blockiest | Block | Blocky | Blockier
exam: In the sentence «the kids laughed at the blocky graphics», what does the author suggest about the pictures? | They were too bright to see | *They looked chunky and not smooth | They were hidden under a blanket | They were smooth and detailed
